WEBVTT

00:03.650 --> 00:07.850
G1 Grand Prix in the Heian Capital!

00:08.490 --> 00:10.570
It's the day we've all been waiting for!

00:10.750 --> 00:12.850
The event that will open a
new door to our history,

00:12.850 --> 00:16.160
the first Ox Cart G1 Grand
Prix in the Heian Capital!

00:16.160 --> 00:33.920
Commentator

00:16.160 --> 00:33.920
Analyst

00:16.490 --> 00:19.040
I, Fujiwara no Teika,
will be your commentator.

00:19.040 --> 00:21.660
Utsunomiya no Yoritsuna
will be your analyst!

00:21.660 --> 00:23.060
I am honored.

00:23.060 --> 00:25.060
Yoritsuna-san, it's finally here.

00:25.060 --> 00:27.110
Yes, this event is supposed

00:27.110 --> 00:29.500
to signal a new beginning for the Heian.

00:29.500 --> 00:30.710
All eyes are watching.

00:31.040 --> 00:33.920
Let's introduce the course, then.

00:34.290 --> 00:36.220
We begin near the Suzaku Palace

00:36.220 --> 00:37.520
and head south on Suzaku Avenue.

00:37.520 --> 00:39.360
After passing through Rashomon,
we head east,

00:39.360 --> 00:41.350
then turn north to cross the Kamo River

00:41.350 --> 00:42.280
and pass Kiyomizu Temple.

00:42.280 --> 00:43.730
There's a pit stop here.

00:43.730 --> 00:45.590
Then we cross the Kamo
River again and head north,

00:45.590 --> 00:47.230
move west on Ichijo Road,

00:47.230 --> 00:48.900
turn left after passing
by the Greater Palace,

00:48.900 --> 00:51.330
and return to Suzaku Avenue
to complete the city course.

00:51.330 --> 00:53.590
Yoritsuna-san, what are the key points?

00:53.590 --> 00:56.500
I believe the slope near Kiyomizu
Temple will be a factor.

00:56.500 --> 00:58.780
Both the climb and the descent
will be treacherous.

00:58.780 --> 01:01.100
The drivers will need
excellent ox control.

01:01.630 --> 01:03.830
Next, we have the starting grid.

01:04.250 --> 01:07.650
At the pole, we have the speedy
playboy, Ariwara no Narihira.

01:07.650 --> 01:10.860
In the front row is the wild young stallion,
the former Emperor Yozei (Sadaakira).

01:10.860 --> 01:14.450
In third, we have the technically
proficient Funya no Yasuhide.

01:14.450 --> 01:17.440
In fourth, we have the Hawk
of Inaba, Ariwara no Yukihira.

01:17.440 --> 01:19.060
In fifth, we have the
hundred-nights-of-ox-carting veteran,

01:19.060 --> 01:20.540
Yoshimine no Munesada.

01:20.540 --> 01:23.850
Finally, we have the Uji
monster, the Monk Kisen.

01:23.850 --> 01:25.850
Otomo no Kuronushi failed to qualify.

01:26.560 --> 01:30.000
Now, who will be the first
champion of this new age?

01:30.000 --> 01:32.320
History is about to be made!

03:02.950 --> 03:09.410
Teika's Room

03:12.940 --> 03:15.340
Fujiwara no Teika

03:13.470 --> 03:14.640
Hello.

03:14.640 --> 03:16.330
It's time for Teika's room.

03:16.680 --> 03:19.920
Today, we have three of Heian's finest.

03:19.920 --> 03:21.530
Ariwara no Narihira-san,

03:19.970 --> 03:25.800
Funya no Yasuhide   Ono no Komachi   Ariwara no Narihira

03:22.040 --> 03:25.070
Ono no Komachi-san, and
Funya no Yasuhide-san.

03:25.440 --> 03:26.350
Hello.

03:26.350 --> 03:27.140
It's a pleasure.

03:27.500 --> 03:28.400
The three of you were

03:28.400 --> 03:30.800
selected as members of
the Six Poetic Geniuses.

03:30.800 --> 03:32.440
In addition, Narihira-san is

03:32.440 --> 03:35.070
the stud who's said to be the
model for Hikaru Genji.

03:35.770 --> 03:37.890
Komachi-san is one of the
three great beauties.

03:38.320 --> 03:41.070
And, uh...

03:41.360 --> 03:43.560
Yasuhide-san is a master of wordplay.

03:43.560 --> 03:45.320
I appreciate the thought.

03:45.800 --> 03:50.170
Here we have a classic
two male, one female group.

03:50.170 --> 03:52.930
Has there been any romantic trouble?

03:52.930 --> 03:53.770
No.

03:54.940 --> 03:56.730
That was a firm denial.

03:56.730 --> 03:59.610
After all, Narihira-sama is a danger

03:59.610 --> 04:00.850
to all women he comes across.

04:00.850 --> 04:04.120
Yes, he's made advances towards

04:04.120 --> 04:05.820
future empresses and sacred maidens.

04:05.820 --> 04:06.930
Sacred maidens?

04:06.930 --> 04:12.850
Imperial Princesses = the Emperor's daughters and sisters

04:07.310 --> 04:09.790
The maidens of highest sanctity

04:09.790 --> 04:12.850
selected from among the Imperial Princesses?

04:13.090 --> 04:14.290
That's amazing.

04:14.690 --> 04:16.900
There are always obstacles in love.

04:16.900 --> 04:19.320
You can't fall in love if you
let yourself be scared away.

04:19.320 --> 04:23.460
That sounds nice and all,
but you're just a player.

04:23.460 --> 04:25.450
Yeah, and he preys on women.

04:25.720 --> 04:27.610
Preys on women?

04:27.610 --> 04:31.290
They'll probably be extinct
by the 21st century.

04:31.290 --> 04:33.750
The goal is to wipe them out.

04:34.120 --> 04:38.100
But shouldn't that make
Komachi-san one of your targets?

04:38.270 --> 04:40.240
Well, let's just say

04:40.240 --> 04:42.880
that I prefer women who are well-endowed.

04:42.880 --> 04:44.260
What's that supposed to mean?

04:45.090 --> 04:48.260
However, nothing ever
works out as planned.

04:48.860 --> 04:54.060
My one true love was only an AA-cup.

04:54.440 --> 04:55.730
What? Is that a problem?

04:56.210 --> 04:59.790
For reference, my brother
Yukihara's wife, Hiroko-dono,

05:00.240 --> 05:01.480
is a G-cup.

05:01.480 --> 05:02.940
How do you know that?!

05:03.280 --> 05:04.450
And Komachi is...

05:09.530 --> 05:11.120
We're finally here.

05:11.120 --> 05:12.370
This is Mount Tsukuba.

05:12.690 --> 05:13.770
Mount Tsukuba!

05:13.770 --> 05:14.960
The stage for many gatherings!

05:15.550 --> 05:17.000
This is the famous place

05:17.000 --> 05:19.070
where men and women have exchanged

05:19.070 --> 05:23.210
poetry and love since
the time of the Manyo!

05:23.210 --> 05:26.010
You're still on a high.

05:26.010 --> 05:27.590
I've always wanted to come here!

05:27.750 --> 05:30.200
We've passed Mikawa,
where I've been assigned,

05:30.200 --> 05:32.230
and traveled far east...

05:33.730 --> 05:36.140
Well, I have a job to do.

05:36.500 --> 05:37.600
That's unfortunate.

05:39.060 --> 05:41.270
We'll finally be alone.

05:43.630 --> 05:46.450
I don't have time for this,

05:46.740 --> 05:50.190
but I can't leave Komachi
and Narihira alone!

05:50.670 --> 05:55.540
Well, since we're here,
let's have a celebration.

05:57.080 --> 05:58.620
You want to have a mixed
party with these members?

05:59.730 --> 06:02.850
Right, we're short one woman.

06:02.850 --> 06:04.860
That's not what I meant.

06:04.860 --> 06:07.690
I'll go find someone else.

06:07.690 --> 06:09.820
The two of you can get started.

06:09.820 --> 06:10.410
What?!

06:10.410 --> 06:11.250
Wait!

06:11.250 --> 06:12.080
Bye.

06:12.080 --> 06:14.610
Honestly, he's so hopeless.

06:14.610 --> 06:17.030
He's dressed like a monk,

06:17.030 --> 06:19.170
so he could try to act like one.

06:19.170 --> 06:21.650
Yeah, I know...

06:21.650 --> 06:24.720
Bastard!  He's too overbearing!

06:25.700 --> 06:27.780
But this is my chance...

06:28.290 --> 06:29.410
Komachi.

06:30.390 --> 06:31.070
Yes?

06:31.540 --> 06:34.280
Uh, actually...

06:34.710 --> 06:38.470
I-I've always been...

06:39.340 --> 06:41.420
In love with you!

06:46.030 --> 06:48.090
Honestly, Yasuhide-sama!

06:48.090 --> 06:50.450
You're such a joker!

06:50.450 --> 06:52.690
Don't make me laugh.

06:52.690 --> 06:54.470
Besides, I only like handsome men.

06:55.300 --> 06:56.540
Still, that's a good idea.

06:56.540 --> 06:58.180
Let's pretend to speak of love.

06:58.330 --> 07:06.070
Pretend

06:59.060 --> 07:02.360
We should come up with a
background story first,

07:02.360 --> 07:05.450
and we'll need to write
love poems to each other.

07:05.450 --> 07:07.070
I'll pretend to be a married woman.

07:07.070 --> 07:09.630
You can be the unfortunate man

07:09.630 --> 07:11.190
who fell in love
with a married woman.

07:12.370 --> 07:14.990
Yes, I'm a very unfortunate man...

07:15.460 --> 07:17.760
Okay, write a poem for me.

07:17.760 --> 07:20.330
Make sure you refer to Mount Tsukuba.

07:20.330 --> 07:21.800
Tsu-Tsukuba...

07:22.570 --> 07:24.240
Great day for fishing,

07:24.240 --> 07:25.730
but nothing's biting.

07:25.730 --> 07:26.550
Fool.

07:28.790 --> 07:31.560
What was that?!
I don't get it!

07:33.250 --> 07:34.930
Please come up with the next verse.

07:34.930 --> 07:35.880
That's impossible!

07:37.430 --> 07:38.370
Lame.

07:39.560 --> 07:42.980
G1 Grand Prix in the Heian Capital!

07:43.380 --> 07:46.340
Yoritsuna-san, whom do you expect to win?

07:46.340 --> 07:48.600
I want to say Narihira,

07:48.600 --> 07:50.910
but instead, I'll pick
his brother Yukihira.

07:50.910 --> 07:52.930
Yoritsuna-san has picked Yukihira!

07:52.930 --> 07:54.780
My hopes are pinned on the Monk Kisen!

07:54.780 --> 07:56.660
Who do you favor?

07:57.390 --> 07:59.210
There's the red signal.

08:03.240 --> 08:04.540
And they're off!

08:07.500 --> 08:13.970
Teika's Room

08:18.000 --> 08:19.680
It's time for Teika's room.

08:20.110 --> 08:21.500
This time, we have the

08:21.500 --> 08:25.900
brilliant general known as the Monk Henjo.

08:23.480 --> 08:25.900
Monk Henjo

08:26.140 --> 08:29.750
After Emperor Ninmyo passed away,

08:29.750 --> 08:31.840
you resigned and abandoned

08:31.840 --> 08:35.860
the name Yoshimine no
Munesada to become Henjo.

08:35.220 --> 08:35.860
Teika-dono.

08:36.190 --> 08:37.140
Yes?

08:37.140 --> 08:41.050
Could you call me Munesada
today, instead of Henjo?

08:41.050 --> 08:42.830
Oh, why?

08:43.430 --> 08:47.000
Henjo is thought of as a perverted monk.

08:47.460 --> 08:49.000
Perverted monk?

08:49.000 --> 08:59.010
The sky is the road home for the holy maidens,
may the wind bring clouds to extend their stay.

08:49.000 --> 09:03.680
The Monk Henjo

08:49.390 --> 08:51.810
Hey, don't you think that the
Monk Henjo is a little perverted?

08:51.810 --> 08:54.410
Yeah, since he wrote about "holy maidens."

08:54.410 --> 08:56.460
There's no excuse for that.

08:56.460 --> 08:58.090
He must have been a perverted monk.

08:58.090 --> 08:58.970
Perverted monk!

08:59.140 --> 08:59.920
A perverted monk!

08:59.920 --> 09:01.550
Because you published my poem

09:01.550 --> 09:03.680
under the name the Monk Henjo.

09:03.940 --> 09:07.970
But that's because you so diligently climbed

09:07.970 --> 09:11.120
to such a high rank among monks.

09:11.660 --> 09:14.990
I wanted to respect that...

09:16.250 --> 09:20.120
I-It's hard with people
who have multiple names,

09:20.120 --> 09:23.700
Lord Kentoku = Fujiwara no Koremasa
Lord Teishin = Fujiwara no Tadahira

09:20.390 --> 09:23.700
such as Lord Teishin and Lord Kentoku.

09:23.910 --> 09:26.830
For most of the women,
I didn't know their real names,

09:26.830 --> 09:29.450
so I had to use nicknames.

09:29.450 --> 09:31.510
Like Sei Shonagon, Murasaki Shikibu,

09:31.510 --> 09:33.700
and Ono no Komachi-dono...

09:33.700 --> 09:35.820
For the mother of General
of the Right, Michitsuna,

09:35.280 --> 09:36.240
Komachi...

09:35.820 --> 09:38.370
I basically put Michitsuna-kun's mom.

09:37.380 --> 09:38.330
He means Yoshiko...

09:39.980 --> 09:42.720
You live in a place that only has women.

09:43.120 --> 09:43.950
Uh-huh.

09:43.950 --> 09:46.950
That's why I love to play with you.

09:46.950 --> 09:47.270
Huh?

09:47.610 --> 09:50.650
They make me play with dolls at home.

09:51.310 --> 09:54.280
You take me outside where it's more fun.

09:54.790 --> 09:58.240
Really?  I feel like I have a little sister.
I'm having fun, too.

09:58.880 --> 09:59.850
Little sister?

10:00.880 --> 10:02.740
Then...  Then...

10:03.170 --> 10:05.590
Can I call you my

10:06.190 --> 10:07.960
dear brother?

10:08.880 --> 10:12.960
After that, Yoshiko and I were
raised as brother and sister.

10:13.420 --> 10:14.540
That's how we grew up.

10:14.950 --> 10:16.000
I see.

10:16.370 --> 10:18.680
That's why you didn't
realize it was love.

10:19.370 --> 10:22.000
Yoshiko always addressed
me as her "dear brother,"

10:22.000 --> 10:24.490
and I didn't mind.

10:24.490 --> 10:27.310
That means she'll have to stop.

10:27.310 --> 10:27.730
Huh?

10:28.000 --> 10:30.700
After you've visited
her one hundred nights,

10:30.700 --> 10:32.140
you'll be getting married, right?

10:32.140 --> 10:34.860
You would address each
other by name then.

10:37.580 --> 10:38.860
Munesada-sama...

10:39.900 --> 10:41.170
Dear brother...

10:42.270 --> 10:43.500
Munesada-san?

10:43.930 --> 10:46.750
I prefer the brother-sister angle.

10:47.110 --> 10:47.580
Huh?

10:48.230 --> 10:49.870
Since there's a touch of taboo involved.

10:49.870 --> 10:52.910
Super-Liberal Interpretation
of the Hyakunin Isshu

10:49.870 --> 10:52.910
Uta-Hen.

10:50.910 --> 10:51.670
What?

10:53.910 --> 10:58.650
We grant dreams and love every night.

10:59.570 --> 11:01.690
Welcome to Host Club Heian.

11:01.690 --> 11:04.640
I am Ariwara no Yukihira, the owner.

11:05.270 --> 11:08.510
I would like to introduce our top hosts.

11:09.100 --> 11:13.520
Our number 5 is the studious
younger brother type, Teika.

11:13.930 --> 11:15.460
He has a knack for getting his way.

11:15.790 --> 11:19.230
Teach me more, ladies.

11:19.230 --> 11:20.570
He's adorable!

11:21.110 --> 11:24.470
Our number 4 is the
entertainer, Yasuhide.

11:24.780 --> 11:26.090
He specializes in wordplay.

11:26.520 --> 11:28.770
Allow me to host you at the host club.

11:28.770 --> 11:30.290
Wow, lame!

11:30.600 --> 11:35.040
Our number 3 is the
self-centered jerk, Sadaakira.

11:35.380 --> 11:37.610
Women beg for him to yell at them.

11:37.610 --> 11:38.880
What are you looking at?!

11:38.880 --> 11:40.740
Get your ass over here, woman!

11:40.740 --> 11:42.630
I want to hear more!

11:42.900 --> 11:46.590
Our number 2 is the friendly
older brother type, Munesada.

11:46.970 --> 11:49.320
He's sensitive and devoted.

11:49.810 --> 11:52.030
Do you mind if I call upon you?

11:52.030 --> 11:53.600
Please!  Please!

11:53.990 --> 11:57.110
Our number 1 host is Narihira.

11:57.490 --> 11:59.770
He will whisper sweet words in your ear.

12:00.530 --> 12:03.570
I offer my heart to you, princess.

12:04.360 --> 12:08.240
My precious one, let us
make love in our dreams.

12:10.020 --> 12:12.010
Hello, Narihira.

12:13.500 --> 12:16.260
Oh, Takaiko.  I've been waiting for you.

12:16.260 --> 12:19.130
You look lovely in that crimson dress.

12:19.480 --> 12:20.320
I'm enthralled.

12:22.800 --> 12:24.800
Ten bottles of Dom Perignon Rose.

12:24.800 --> 12:27.260
One order for pink champagne!

12:25.010 --> 12:35.020
In the sleepy spring sunlight,
Rosy Dom and Perignon.

12:28.310 --> 12:34.020
A wealth of love awaits
you at Host Club Heian.

12:35.260 --> 12:38.770
G1 Grand Prix in the Heian Capital!

12:40.780 --> 12:47.280
Teika's Room

12:51.260 --> 12:52.070
Hello.

12:52.070 --> 12:54.120
I am your host, Fujiwara no Teika.

12:54.120 --> 12:56.900
I am his assistant,
Utsunomiya no Yoritsuna.

12:56.900 --> 12:59.400
Today, we have a married
couple as our guests.

12:59.400 --> 13:00.710
And they're newlyweds.

13:00.710 --> 13:04.080
Uh-oh, I'm expecting some sappy talk.

13:04.080 --> 13:05.850
Let's bring them in then.

13:06.280 --> 13:07.560
Husband and wife.

13:07.560 --> 13:08.970
Come on down!

13:10.150 --> 13:11.590
The Former Emperor Yozei,

13:10.220 --> 13:14.060
Former Emperor Yozei       Wife, Yasuko

13:11.590 --> 13:14.260
also known as Sadaakira-san, and Yasuko-san!

13:14.260 --> 13:15.190
Hello.

13:15.640 --> 13:19.020
I believe that you've known each
other since you were children.

13:19.290 --> 13:20.080
Indeed.

13:20.080 --> 13:22.760
Were you attracted to
each other back then?

13:22.760 --> 13:23.930
I'm not sure.

13:23.930 --> 13:26.790
In hindsight, that may
have been the case.

13:26.790 --> 13:28.820
Keep your mouth shut, frog girl.

13:29.600 --> 13:33.390
Oh, that was, "I love you, honey."

13:33.390 --> 13:34.040
Huh?

13:34.040 --> 13:34.790
Really?

13:35.090 --> 13:35.880
Yes.

13:35.880 --> 13:38.150
Stop making shit up, you sow!

13:38.150 --> 13:39.350
I'll chop you up and cook you!

13:39.350 --> 13:42.880
That was, "You're so cute
that I could eat you up."

13:42.880 --> 13:44.010
Ah...

13:44.240 --> 13:46.340
Hey, ugly!  If you keep talking,

13:46.340 --> 13:47.900
I'll string you up in the pond all night!

13:47.900 --> 13:48.470
What?

13:48.920 --> 13:50.510
Th-That was,

13:51.210 --> 13:53.730
"I'm not going to let you go tonight."

13:54.330 --> 13:54.890
We're leaving!

13:54.890 --> 13:55.430
Huh?

13:55.760 --> 13:57.350
I'm tired!

13:57.350 --> 13:58.650
What?  Already?

13:59.180 --> 14:00.360
You want to as soon as we get home?

14:00.360 --> 14:02.370
Stop talking!  Do you
want me to gag you?!

14:02.370 --> 14:03.680
How would you like it tonight?

14:03.680 --> 14:04.230
Shut up!

14:04.730 --> 14:06.780
G1 Grand Prix!

14:06.780 --> 14:14.120
Commentator

14:06.780 --> 14:14.120
Analyst

14:07.210 --> 14:08.910
I am Teika, your commentator.

14:08.910 --> 14:10.600
The race is halfway through

14:10.600 --> 14:12.710
and the racers have made their pit stops!

14:12.710 --> 14:14.120
Let's go to Yoritsuna-san on the scene!

14:14.860 --> 14:16.290
Yoritsuna-san.

14:16.620 --> 14:19.360
Yes, this is Yoritsuna
at Kiyomizu Temple.

14:19.360 --> 14:21.460
Can you tell us what's going on there?

14:21.750 --> 14:24.920
Yes, the crews are
finishing up their work.

14:25.220 --> 14:28.000
Munesada-sama, we've finished
changing the tires.

14:28.000 --> 14:28.470
Yes.

14:28.780 --> 14:31.100
Narihira-sama, please have some water.

14:31.100 --> 14:33.210
Have some sweets, as well.

14:33.210 --> 14:35.610
Damn you, Narihira!

14:34.010 --> 14:35.260
Thank you.

14:35.610 --> 14:38.270
A general dares to stand ahead of me?

14:38.820 --> 14:39.890
In that case...

14:40.390 --> 14:41.540
Hey, Yasuko!

14:41.540 --> 14:43.320
What is it, Sadaakira-sama?

14:43.320 --> 14:44.520
Bring me sake.

14:44.520 --> 14:46.260
Sake?

14:46.260 --> 14:48.400
Let the ox drink some.
It'll restore his energy.

14:49.090 --> 14:51.290
Is this really a good idea?

14:58.350 --> 14:59.200
What's going on?

15:01.070 --> 15:02.420
We have a crash!

15:02.420 --> 15:03.560
The pit is in chaos!

15:03.560 --> 15:05.340
This is big trouble!

15:05.650 --> 15:12.090
Teika's Room

15:16.010 --> 15:17.400
This is Teika's Room.

15:17.400 --> 15:20.390
Our last guest is Fujiwara no Kinto-san,

15:20.390 --> 15:22.320
a great poet of the mid-Heian era.

15:22.000 --> 15:23.940
Fujiwara no Kinto

15:22.640 --> 15:23.940
So, Teika-kun...

15:24.460 --> 15:26.360
Yes, what is it?

15:26.360 --> 15:28.980
Why did you call me here?

15:29.710 --> 15:32.980
Everybody else here has
already been on this show,

15:32.980 --> 15:34.530
while this is my first time.

15:35.150 --> 15:38.200
I'm not too happy about this
being my first appearance.

15:38.710 --> 15:40.990
W-Well, you see...

15:40.990 --> 15:44.180
We'll be moving on to
the mid-Heian era next,

15:44.180 --> 15:49.260
so I invited you as a
representative of that period.

15:50.800 --> 15:53.030
Then shouldn't you have invited

15:53.030 --> 15:55.970
Chancellor of the Realm
Fujiwara no Michinaga?

15:56.750 --> 16:00.460
At the time, you played
a significant role

16:00.460 --> 16:03.270
in To Shikibu changing her
name to Murasaki Shikibu,

16:03.270 --> 16:05.530
and you were also involved
with Sei Shonagon,

16:05.530 --> 16:07.110
author of the <i>Pillow Book</i>.

16:07.550 --> 16:13.270
So I felt that you were a perfect choice,
as a cultural leader of the period.

16:14.440 --> 16:17.800
The title of "leader" sounds a bit
too high and mighty for my tastes,

16:18.260 --> 16:20.250
but I suppose that you're right.

16:20.250 --> 16:23.440
Since I excel at poetry,
literature, and music,

16:22.180 --> 16:25.230
Whew, he's in a better mood now.

16:23.440 --> 16:26.710
I can understand why you
would consider me a leader.

16:27.120 --> 16:28.380
By the way, Teika-kun.

16:28.380 --> 16:29.340
Oh, yes.

16:29.820 --> 16:31.980
The standards you followed

16:31.980 --> 16:35.510
for the Hyakunin Isshu
were slightly weak.

16:35.510 --> 16:36.800
Really?

16:37.230 --> 16:40.720
I wouldn't have included Yakamochi's
"When the Misty Bridge,"

16:40.720 --> 16:42.970
and I don't understand how you ignored

16:42.970 --> 16:47.020
Prince Tomohira, who was later
considered a literary genius.

16:47.650 --> 16:50.550
Plus, 43 of the 100 poems are love poems,

16:50.550 --> 16:52.550
so it's not very balanced.

16:52.550 --> 16:56.160
I realize that you compiled it for
a kinsman living in seclusion,

16:56.160 --> 16:59.950
but is it appropriate to fill the
collection with poems about love?

17:00.490 --> 17:02.250
Do you believe that you're...

17:05.540 --> 17:07.190
Wh-What was that for?!

17:08.450 --> 17:09.410
Tee-hee.

17:09.410 --> 17:11.260
You have a serious attitude problem!

17:11.620 --> 17:15.600
How dare you punch the
great councilor Kinto?!

17:15.600 --> 17:18.900
In that case, I will defeat

17:18.900 --> 17:21.140
your Hyakunin Isshu
with my Sanjurokuninsen!

17:21.140 --> 17:23.700
Heian

17:22.720 --> 17:27.370
The Heian Poet Card Battle, Teika vs. Kinto!

17:23.700 --> 17:27.810
Poet Card Battle

17:28.150 --> 17:30.250
The Heian Poet Card Battle is a game

17:30.250 --> 17:34.170
where each poet card has
been assigned a power value.

17:34.760 --> 17:36.460
Each player starts with
30,000 Soul Points.

17:36.460 --> 17:40.010
The player who reduces his opponent
to zero Soul Points first wins.

17:40.010 --> 17:43.370
The player also wins if his
opponent runs out of cards first.

17:43.670 --> 17:47.220
The battlefield has attack
zones and defense zones.

17:47.220 --> 17:49.450
Once a poet has been summoned
to the attack zone,

17:49.450 --> 17:52.050
it's allowed to attack in the next turn

17:52.050 --> 17:54.940
in the opponent's attack
zone or the player.

17:55.370 --> 17:58.720
Poets summoned to the
defense zone cannot attack,

17:58.720 --> 18:01.690
but they can defend when
the opponent attacks.

18:02.070 --> 18:04.560
The player is also allowed to spend

18:04.560 --> 18:07.620
100 Soul Points at the
beginning of his turn

18:07.620 --> 18:09.060
to move a poet between zones.

18:09.600 --> 18:11.630
Each poet has a power value.

18:11.630 --> 18:13.010
When poets battle,

18:13.010 --> 18:14.860
the poet with the higher
power value wins.

18:14.860 --> 18:17.290
The defeated poet will
be sent to the graveyard.

18:17.290 --> 18:19.680
When the poets have equal
power, it's a draw,

18:19.680 --> 18:22.030
and they're both sent to the graveyard.

18:22.030 --> 18:23.380
When summoning a poet,

18:23.380 --> 18:25.900
the player must pay half the poet's
power value in Soul Points.

18:25.900 --> 18:29.000
It's riskier to summon Poets
with higher power values.

18:29.700 --> 18:32.040
The player recovers 1,000 Soul Points

18:32.040 --> 18:33.470
after the draw phase of his turn.

18:33.470 --> 18:35.690
However, the max is 30,000.

18:35.690 --> 18:38.800
Also, there are Poets
with special abilities.

18:39.240 --> 18:43.390
The key is to choose the right
poets when building a deck.

18:43.540 --> 18:45.040
Turn 1, Kinto!

18:45.440 --> 18:46.320
Draw.

18:46.920 --> 18:49.600
I summon Nakatsukasa to the defense zone.

18:49.600 --> 18:50.690
End turn.

18:51.000 --> 18:52.620
Turn 2, Teika!

18:52.620 --> 18:53.530
Draw.

18:54.280 --> 18:56.960
I summon Funya no Yasuhide
to the attack zone.

18:56.960 --> 18:58.200
End turn.

18:58.600 --> 19:00.290
Turn 3, Kinto!

19:00.290 --> 19:01.250
Draw.

19:02.020 --> 19:03.120
End turn.

19:03.400 --> 19:05.060
Turn 4, Teika!

19:03.400 --> 19:05.060
He didn't do anything...

19:05.060 --> 19:05.900
Draw.

19:06.590 --> 19:09.240
I summon Harumichi no Tsuraki
to the defense zone.

19:09.240 --> 19:11.170
I attack the player with Yasuhide.

19:11.560 --> 19:12.900
I take the damage.

19:13.420 --> 19:15.020
He didn't block my attack?

19:13.760 --> 19:15.460
Turn 5, Kinto!

19:15.700 --> 19:16.300
Draw.

19:17.370 --> 19:18.550
End turn.

19:18.780 --> 19:19.940
He's not taking me seriously.

19:18.780 --> 19:20.710
Turn 6, Teika!

19:20.710 --> 19:21.550
Draw!

19:21.950 --> 19:23.760
I move Tsuraki to the attack zone.

19:24.090 --> 19:26.620
I summon Advisor Takamura
to the defense zone!

19:26.620 --> 19:29.850
Then I attack the player
with Yasuhide and Tsuraki!

19:30.350 --> 19:31.750
I take the damage.

19:31.750 --> 19:33.720
Turn 7, Kinto!

19:33.720 --> 19:34.690
Draw.

19:35.830 --> 19:37.690
Teika-kun, you've lost.

19:37.980 --> 19:40.530
I move Nakatsukasa to the attack zone.

19:40.900 --> 19:42.730
Then I activate the card's ability.

19:42.730 --> 19:44.480
When the player has less
than 10,000 Soul Points,

19:44.480 --> 19:47.490
the cost to summon Manyo
poets is reduced to 1/10.

19:47.850 --> 19:50.250
I summon Yamabe no Akahito,
Otomo no Yakamochi,

19:50.250 --> 19:53.130
and Kakinomoto no Hitomaro
to the defense zone.

19:53.430 --> 19:55.020
I see!  This was his strategy!

19:55.020 --> 19:58.630
Plus, I activate the
Sanjurokuninsen ability.

19:58.630 --> 20:01.430
Add 1,000 power for each additional poet.

20:01.730 --> 20:04.070
Nakatsukasa's power increases to 10,000.

20:04.070 --> 20:05.550
I attack the player!

20:06.390 --> 20:07.750
I block with Takamura!

20:08.740 --> 20:10.590
Turn 8, Teika!

20:08.740 --> 20:10.590
I need to defend or I'll lose!

20:11.170 --> 20:11.900
Draw.

20:12.720 --> 20:14.700
Move Yasuhide to the defense zone,

20:15.220 --> 20:16.460
and I use the Monk ability to

20:16.460 --> 20:18.050
send Tsuraki to the graveyard

20:18.050 --> 20:20.370
and summon the Monk Kisen at no cost.

20:20.370 --> 20:21.650
The Six Poetic Genius bonus

20:21.650 --> 20:23.320
increases their power by 2,000.

20:23.710 --> 20:25.570
Then I summon Narihira

20:25.950 --> 20:27.300
and his power increases by 2,000.

20:27.690 --> 20:29.950
Narihira also benefits from
the Sanjurokuninsen ability

20:29.950 --> 20:31.470
and gains an additional 4,000 power.

20:31.470 --> 20:34.420
Finally, I summon myself and end my turn.

20:34.420 --> 20:36.450
You've managed to stabilize.

20:34.850 --> 20:36.450
Turn 9, Kinto!

20:36.450 --> 20:37.640
However, every poet in my deck

20:37.640 --> 20:39.510
was a member of the Sanjurokunin.

20:39.890 --> 20:41.970
My power will continue to increase.

20:42.310 --> 20:43.150
Draw.

20:43.590 --> 20:45.770
I move Nakatsukasa to the defense zone.

20:45.770 --> 20:49.120
Then I summon Minamoto no
Shitago and end my turn.

20:49.840 --> 20:51.480
Now, it's your turn.

20:51.730 --> 20:53.390
He's going to overwhelm me at this rate.

20:52.450 --> 20:54.380
Turn 10, Teika!

20:54.000 --> 20:55.130
What do I do?!

20:55.130 --> 20:56.050
Teika...

20:58.230 --> 21:00.130
Sing for me, Teika...

21:01.790 --> 21:02.780
Draw.

21:03.620 --> 21:06.380
Kinto-senpai, you lose.

21:06.380 --> 21:07.220
What?

21:07.450 --> 21:09.010
I move myself to the attack zone!

21:09.590 --> 21:13.210
I summon Princess Shokushi
to the defense zone!

21:13.600 --> 21:15.950
I activate the ability Teika Jasmine!

21:15.950 --> 21:18.670
All other poets are unable to act!

21:18.670 --> 21:21.340
There's nobody to defend you now!

21:21.580 --> 21:22.470
What?!

21:22.470 --> 21:23.280
Prepare yourself!

21:23.970 --> 21:26.340
As I wait!

21:26.340 --> 21:27.050
That's enough.

21:28.420 --> 21:30.370
Oh, Tsurayuki-senpai.

21:30.370 --> 21:31.810
You shouldn't fight.

21:32.080 --> 21:35.870
You're both excellent poets,
so you should be friends.

21:35.870 --> 21:36.520
Right?

21:36.520 --> 21:37.170
Uh...

21:37.170 --> 21:38.710
Understood!

21:38.710 --> 21:41.420
Teika-kun, your Hyakunin
Isshu is beautiful!

21:41.420 --> 21:43.280
Let's talk poetry again some time!

21:43.280 --> 21:44.090
R-Right...

21:44.090 --> 21:45.900
So, Tsurayuki-senpai,

21:45.900 --> 21:47.560
could you give me your autograph?

21:48.930 --> 21:51.870
G1 Grand Prix Final!

21:52.090 --> 21:53.510
The crash isn't over yet!

21:53.510 --> 21:54.890
The pit is still a mess!

21:56.270 --> 21:57.930
Yoritsuna-san, give us an update!

21:58.390 --> 21:59.630
One of the carts has pulled ahead!

22:00.100 --> 22:01.840
It's Munesada-san's cart!

22:01.840 --> 22:03.520
This is nothing compared

22:03.520 --> 22:06.460
to the hundred nights
I spent making visits.

22:07.550 --> 22:10.600
Yoshiko, I dedicate this victory to you.

22:10.600 --> 22:12.980
Yoshimine no Munesada
has escaped the chaos

22:12.980 --> 22:15.520
and heads for the Kamo River
at an incredible pace!

22:15.950 --> 22:18.020
Victory and Yoshiko are both mine!

22:20.070 --> 22:20.900
What?

22:21.550 --> 22:23.820
All racers are out!

22:24.100 --> 22:26.560
This ended the same way
as his hundred nights.

22:26.560 --> 22:30.160
Next time, we have Ox Cart
G1 Grand Prix in Dazaifu!

22:30.160 --> 22:31.400
And with that...

22:31.400 --> 22:32.870
Good-bye, everyone!

22:32.870 --> 22:34.870
Stupid

22:32.870 --> 22:34.870
Poetic Tale 6:

22:32.870 --> 22:34.870
END

24:04.920 --> 24:20.700
Next
Episode

24:04.920 --> 24:20.700
Yoshitaka & the Daughter
of Minamoto
no Yasumitsu

24:04.920 --> 24:20.700
Fujiwara no Yoshitaka

24:07.370 --> 24:12.010
For you, I would have given up my life.

24:12.840 --> 24:15.860
Now together, I guard it dear.
